# Adaptive and Responsive Design Implementation Plan

The objective is to ensure the GHG Reporting application is fully functional and visually appealing on tablets and mobile devices.

## Proposed Changes

### [CSS Layer]

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard-dark.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard-dark.css)
- **Global Reset**: Ensure `box-sizing: border-box` is applied to all elements to prevent padding from increasing element sizes beyond their container.
- **Fluid Layout**:
    - Change fixed widths and paddings to use relative units or more flexible grid values.
    - Fix the `.app-container` and `.main-content` to ensure they fit exactly within `100vh` without causing vertical/horizontal scrollbars on the body.
    - Adjust `.dashboard-grid` columns for smaller desktops (e.g., laptop screens) using `minmax` or percentages instead of fixed `2fr 1fr` if it's too cramped.
- **Mobile Responsiveness**:
    - Add media queries for Tablet (`max-width: 1024px`) and Mobile (`max-width: 768px`).
    - **Sidebar**: Switch to a drawer (overlay) mode on tablets and mobile.
    - **Grid**: Stack dashboard cards into a single column on mobile.
- **Components**:
    - Ensure tables have `overflow-x: auto` containers.
    - Make card heights more flexible.

### [Javascript Layer]

#### [NEW] [mobile-menu.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/mobile-menu.js)
- Implement a script to toggle the mobile sidebar.
- Add window resize listeners to handle state transitions between desktop/mobile layouts.

### [HTML Layer]

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html), [emission-selection.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-selection.html), [emission-factor.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-factor.html)
- Add a hamburger menu icon to the top bar.
- Ensure consistent viewport meta tag (already present).
- Link `mobile-menu.js`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Use the browser tool to verify the presence of the toggle button and test clicking it on mobile resolutions.

### Manual Verification
- Resize the browser window to verify all breakpoints.
- Check that the dashboard grid stacks correctly.
- Ensure the sidebar drawer opens and closes as expected on mobile.
- Verify horizontal scrolling for tables.
